From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:29:33 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 25/79] runner: the frontend from checked Python/calc code to
 calc firmware or a circuit ELF

Second slice of the in-thinking runner port, from the DSV41
release branch (7b79ef92d) unchanged: runner_frontend*.zig and its C runtime
sources lower a checked Python/calc subset (integers, decimals, fractions,
collections, loops, defs) to calc firmware or an RV32 circuit ELF, with cost
budgets and an ELF cache. Model-independent; nothing in the engine imports it.

Build: test-runner-frontend-host (in test-cuda-host). The parts that need the
graph bank (inline integer cells and their def/list/loop tests) come with it;
the boot self-test executable and the scanner regression test come with the
runner core.

Two changes from the branch: the forkserver shim (C code the configured clang
builds at warm-up) moves to runner_frontend_forkserver_shim.c, embedded with the
same bytes, so its getenv of the inherited socket fd is not read as a Zig engine
setting; and the spawn timers read the monotonic clock through libc, so the
module compiles for macOS (its Linux syscalls stay behind the posix_spawn check).
